    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (71.80) and **Bryce Harper** (70.17) stand out as our elite pivots. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against the mid-rotation xERA of Miles Mikolas, coupled with a rare \"wind-out\" advantage and a slow delivery profile that significantly bolsters his stolen base potential. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** is positioned to feast on the weaker side of a platoon advantage against Justin Wrobleski, with wind conditions and a premium spot in the order driving his score well into the upper echelon. **Luis Arraez** also warrants mention; while he lacks the home run upside of the power hitters, his elite contact skills against the shaky Luinder Avila and an leadoff assignment make him a cornerstone for our AVG category integrity.\n\nThe rotation selection was particularly tight regarding the utilization of **Daulton Varsho**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 50.95 efficiency score. While his platoon edge against Drew Rasmussen is favorable, the optimizer opted for **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.63) and **Taylor Ward** (60.72) due to superior overall matchup profiles. **Gleyber Torres** (64.55) remains a high-variance play; while he holds a strong score, we must monitor the 41% rain risk in his park, as any delay could dampen the production of an otherwise favorable matchup against David Peterson. Likewise, **Tyler Freeman** carries a 33% rain risk, and though the efficiency metrics support starting him, the weather volatility serves as the primary threat to his high-projected output.",
